SEALING TECHNIQUE - FOUR-CORNER / FIVE-SEAL BARRIER
Perimeter defence for a sealing site or hideout entrance.

Where an extraction or hideout must be shielded from intruders, members deploy a
sealing barrier anchored by paper talismans placed at the corners of the protected
space, typically upon four surrounding surfaces plus a central marker.

- Each talisman is a physical anchor. The barrier holds while all remain in place.
- The barrier cannot be broken from within by ordinary force, nor breached from
  without until every anchoring talisman is removed - and the anchors are hidden at
  a distance from the barrier itself, often disguised in the surrounding terrain.
- Removing the talismans simultaneously is required; pulling one alone can trigger a
  trapped counter-seal on the remover.

Use to buy the three days a full extraction demands. An intruder who reaches the
chamber before the barrier falls has already cost us time we do not spend twice.
